Workstation V1.93a, Plus V2.90: never released


Workstation V1.94x, Plus V2.91 include following major changes (19 FEB 89):

1) Completed Motorola DSP5600x FFT acceleration for Loughborough Sound Images
   (LSI) board (WORKSTATION SOFTWARE ONLY)

2) MINIMAL A/D and D/A for Motorola DSP5600x LSI board (either channel 1 OR
   channel 2 operation, no triggering, no two-channel operation, sampling rates
   limited to between 20 KHz and 30 KHz, depending on host machine speed)
   (WORKSTATION SOFTWARE ONLY)

3) Crosshair cursor and amplitude read-out of individual points in time wave-
   form display, magnitude frame display, and phase display.  Point-read out
   is controllable from a "fine", point-by-point mode, to a more "coarse"
   point-skip mode.

4) Addition of "point" display as a selection of the "Units" command ('U' key).
   All time, magnitude frame, and phase units display can now be displayed as
   "xxxx Pt", in addition to msec, KHz, etc.  The fourth selection of 'U' in-
   vokes point display.

5) Any scaling required in forward and inverse FFT operations is now main-
   tained automatically in the waveform header, allowing all non-dB frequency
   domain waveforms to be compared easily.  Also, pre-FFT divide-by-FFT
   order scaling has been eliminated (see Users Manual).

6) Motorola DSP56001 filter source code generations no longer store variables
   at X:FFFE or X:FFFF, and no longer include "X:" or "Y:" in equate state-
   ments, since Motorola decided to cease supporting this feature in versions
   of their assembler after 2.01.

7) Maximum FIR filter coefficients for all DSP chip FIR source code generation
   has been extended to 2048, unless restricted by the memory capacity of an
   individual chip.


Workstation V1.94a, Plus V2.91a (27 FEB 89):

1) Bug-fix to increased length FIR filter lengths in machine-generated source
   code and simulated DSP-chip impulse response.


Workstation V1.94b, Plus V2.91b include following major changes (2 MAR 89):

1) Magnitude and 3-D Spectrogram non-log displays now show amplitude (y-axis)
   units that have automatically been divided by the time domain analysis
   framesize and multiplied by two for real-valued (non-complex) input time
   waveforms.  No multiplication by two is performed for complex input time
   wvaeforms.  Thus, a pure sinusoidal input time waveform of amplitude A
   will also show amplitude A at its fundamental frequency for magnitude
   (squareroot of sum-of-squares) display.

2) Magnitude and 3-D Spectrogram displays also have been changed to allow
   entry of a y-axis scaling factor and label, as in time domain display.
   A field has been added to the data entry menus of these functions to
   accommodate this change.

3) Forward FFT generation, Magnitude, Phase, 3-D Spectrogram and 2-D Spectro-
   graph display have been modified to process and show BOTH sides of the
   spectrum in the case of complex input time waveforms to the FFT function.
   Sorry for the oversight.


Hypersignal-Plus V2.91c includes following major changes (6 MAR 89):

1) 2-D Spectrograph drawing speed is up to twice as fast, depending on drawing
   complexity (contour, time shown, etc.) and machine configuration (80x87,
   instruction cache memory, etc.).

2) File Acquisition is much faster, owing to new write-to-disk scheme that
   dynamically switches from disk-writing individual samples to 1000-pt
   frames, if the input format allows it (this has already been in Hyper-
   signal-Workstation for some time).


Hypersignal-Workstation V1.94c includes following major changes (8 MAR 89):

1) 2-D Spectrograph drawing speed is up to twice as fast, depending on drawing
   complexity (contour, time shown, etc.) and machine configuration (80x87,
   instruction cache memory, etc.).

2) Digital Oscilloscope functions have revamped scaling on both the time
   and amplitude axes that attempt to use, depending on the current value
   of sampling frequency chosen, more readable values.  For example, scaling
   now progresses as 10 msec/Div, 5 msec/Div, 2 msec/Div, etc.

   Initial trigger values can now be entered in the data entry menu, allowing
   easier one-shot operation.

   Triggering inside the scope function, using the '+' and '-' keys, has
   increased resolution, allowing finer control.

   Also, a "freeze" function (use the 'F' key) that enables print-out and
   waveform capture to disk file has been installed.  Finally, a few bugs
   have been fixed and more efficient DSP board memory utilization has been
   achieved.


Workstation V1.94d, Plus V2.91d (22 MAR 89):

1) Bug fix in integer-precision inverse FFT functions (including fixed-point
   DSP chip board acceleration versions).

2) More LSI board DSP5600x stuff:

   - D/A had some bugs fixed, and is now also active from time and 2-D spec-
     trographic displays.

   - Inverse FFT is complete and fully operational.

   - Digital Scope is complete and fully operational.

   - All transfer rates between host PC and LSI DSP56001 board have been
     DRAMATICALLY improved (owing to some novel transfer techniques to
     compensate for the unusual and awkward "host interface" and larger
     buffer sizes).  A/D rates have been measured at above 100 KHz for
     a 20 MHz 386 machine with a vanilla hard disk and controller (avg.
     access time 25msec).  That means over 45 KHz continuous to hard
     disk for two-channel (stereo) applications!

   - A/D "Analog Conversion" function is our most flexible yet for a 
     DSP chip-based board, allowing such scenarios as one channel used
     solely for triggering (no data collected), collecting data on both
     the trigger channel and data channel, etc.

3) Crosshair cursor amplitude read-out (righthand side of display) in time
   and phase displays now shows all 5 digits for negative numbers larger
   than 9999.

4) Bug fix in both DSP32 and all TMS320C25 real-time power spectra analyzer
   display (was accidentally introduced with enhancement 3) from 2 MAR, above).


Workstation V1.94e, Plus V2.91e (30 MAR 89):

1) Another bug-fix in inverse FFT (only affected very long files).

2) File Acquisition hex format function has been modified to NOT consider the
   'x' character in hex formats of the type '0xABCD' as a separator character.
   In effect, '0x' in hex formats is now ignored.

3) Hypersignal-Workstation and Hypersignal-Plus now have an optional "exten-
   ded-length" waveform header of 64 integers in addition to the standard
   10 integers.  If bit 2 in the waveform header 'data type' attribute is
   set, then the program assumes a header 64 integers long.

4) NOTE! NOTE! NOTE!  Workstation 1.94e has known bug where sampling fre-
   quencies below about 100 Hz cause normal time-domain and frequency-
   domain functions to experience a run-time error when loading waveforms
   for processing/display.  This problem has already been fixed, but version
   1.94f was not final-tested soon enough for the quarterly update.  If you
   encounter this problem, just call to receive version 1.94f.


Workstation V1.94f (3 APR 89):

1) Low sampling-frequency error (above) fixed.

2) Problem in scope and analyzer where dual-display horizontal axes lines
   do not always display correctly fixed.

Workstation V1.94g, Plus V2.91f (28 APR 89):

1) Problem in digital scope "input range" field corrected where only values
   up to 5 Volts were being accepted.  Maximum value for most hardware is
   now 20 (Workstation only).

2) TMS320C25 and TMS32020 FIR filter source code corrections:

   1) Equate statement for XN variable corrected to so as to be placed
      at beginning of delay taps in block B0 memory (instead of at location
      zero).

   2) Missing instructions for saving of status added to FILT routine.

   3) Resetting of current page instruction inserted in commented-out test
      example AFTER call to INIT.

   4) NOTE: Not really a change, but keep in mind that "Base Address.."
      field on Code Generation menu still controls location of YN and
      ONE variables, independently of location of XN variable.

3) CAC32 spectrum analyzer function now includes complete, dual-channel
   scaling along vertical axis.


Workstation V1.94h, Plus V2.91g (8 MAY 89):

1) "Pop" at end of D/A playback for DSP56001 hardware fixed (Workstation only).

2) 2-D spectrograph D/A playback-followed-by-zoom bug fixed for DSP56001 hard-
   ware (Workstation only).

3) Binary-ASCII-Binary conversion now produces and accepts ASCII hexadecimal
   and floating-point formats in addition to ASCII decimal format.

4) File Acquisition function now allows up to 16-bit masking for incoming
   samples in all formats except for ASCII hexadecimal, in which case up to
   32-bit masking (shifting) is allowed.

5) Difference Equations now has min & max operators.  For example, to use
   the minimum of elements A and B in an equation, type "A<B".  To find
   the maximum, type "A>B".  Order of the two elements is unimportant. The
   precedence level of this operation is high, immediately after exponentia-
   tion (raising something to a power).  Thus, max's and min's are evaluated
   BEFORE multiplication, division, addition, and subtraction.

   For example, to generate a third waveform that is the max of two input
   waveforms, an equation like the following would work:

      y[n]=x1[n]>x2[n]


Workstation V1.94i, Plus V2.91h (21 MAY 89):

1) "ADDK" instruction in TMS32020 IIR filter generated code for "INIT" routine
   replaced by "ADLK", which is legitimate 32020 instruction.

2) File Acquisition problem with Motorola DSP56001 software simulator hex
   file output fixed.

3) Some spectrum analyzer functions that were not adjusting sampling frequency
   by factor of 2 for two-channel operation corrected (Workstation only).

4) Spectrum analyzer function for LSI DSP56001 board added (Workstation only).

5) Failure of graphical filter design functions to properly re-initialize from
   file once in display mode corrected (this problem may not exist before
   Workstation V1.94f and Plus V2.91e).

6) Failure of 2-D spectrograph to automatically flip trace 2 when one of the
   displayed waveforms is LPC autocorrelated data corrected.


Workstation V1.94j, Plus V2.91i (6 JUN 89):

1) On-line HELP updated.  Hypersignal-Plus Utilities Column menu structure
   re-arranged to be more compatible with Hypersignal-Workstation for pur-
   poses of HELP file maintenance.  Because of this, it is STRONGLY SUGGESTED
   THAT YOU DELETE YOUR PREVIOUS HSPLUS.CNF FILE BEFORE USING HYPERSIGNAL-
   PLUS V2.91j.

2) Waveform editing speed increased by a factor of 14.  A million-sample file
   that used to take 20 minutes to edit on a 12 MHz AT clone now takes less
   than a minute and a half.

3) Memory-usage error corrected in Parks-McClellan FIR design where filters
   longer than 208-210 taps were not converging.


Workstation V1.95a, Plus V2.92a (30 JUN 89):

1) Log frequency-axis added to graphical filter design dispays.  Use 'L' key
   to produce all four combinations of log-linear for the amplitude and
   frequency axes.  Also, use the 'G' key to extend the x and y grid tic
   marks fully across the display.

2) Problem where LSI DSP56000 spectrum analyzer would occasionally glitch and
   hang-up corrected.

3) First level of Motorola ADS DSP56000 board support is installed (DSP Acc-
   elerator function active).  Use 'ADS56-A' for System Configuration selec-
   tion ('-A' is for Ariel ADC56000 card, '-B' is for Motorola ADC16 card).

   PLEASE NOTE THAT YOU MUST HAVE A "HYPER-ADM" CARD INSTALLED INSIDE YOUR
   PC IN ADDITION TO THE MOTOROLA ADM CARD.  BOTH ARE THEN CONNECTED DIRECTLY
   TO THE ADS BOARD.  YOU MAY EITHER PURCHASE THE "HYPER-ADM" CARD FROM
   HYPERCEPTION OR BUILD YOUR OWN (WE WILL PROVIDE THE SCHEMATIC AND PARTS
   LIST).

4) Previous-release (6 JUN 89, above) waveform editor enhancement had problem
   where waveform files were sometimes not "sewn" back together properly. This
   has been corrected.

   HYPERSIGNAL-WORKSTATION NOTE:

   INTEGRATION OF MOTOROLA ADS HARDWARE CAUSED CHANGE TO SYSTEM CONFIGURATION
   MENU LAY-OUT. IT IS SUGGESTED THAT YOU DELETE YOUR CURRENT HSWORK.CNF FILE
   BEFORE RUNNING 1.95A.  ALTERNATIVELY, YOU MAY SWITCH THE DATA IN THE "I/O
   BASEADDRESS" AND "MEMORY BASEADDRESS" FIELDS.


Workstation V1.95b, Plus V2.92b (5 JUL 89):

1) Extra minus sign for program-generated TMS320C25 IIR filter (structure 3)
   source code fixed.  Because IIR coefficient B2 needed to be stored as neg-
   ative, B2 coefficients that actually were negative had two minus signs--
   unfortunately, the TI assembler does not evaluate "minus * minus" as plus.


Workstation V1.95c, Plus V2.92c (7 JUL 89):

1) Criterion for truncation of IIR Filter Construction impulse response wave-
   form output changed from decay of 1/100 of maximum amplitude to decay of
   1/1000 of maximum amplitude.  Frequency responses after FFT processing may
   show up to 20 dB improvement, depending on type of filter and specifica-
   tions.  Other effects of truncation also greatly mitigated, including
   flatness of passband in "maximally flat" designs (e.g. Butterworth), and
   shape of low-amplitude ripples in Chebychev II and elliptic designs.

2) Problem in IIR Filter Construction corrected where bandstop filters with
   transition bandwidths much larger than the stopband region caused run-
   time error.


Workstation V1.95d, Plus V2.92d (12 JUL 89):

1) Labeling problem for 3-D spectrogram where negative log value for y-axis
   was not displayed in the proper location corrected.

2) Correction to IIR Filter Construction bandpass and bandstop filters where
   gain factor ("constant multiplier C") was not being calculated correctly.
   All Hypersignal-Plus and -Workstation filters now correctly produce unity
   gain in passband regions.

3) Correlation option added to Convolution function. Use CONVOLVE/CORRELATE
   menu field to specify which.

4) Dual-waveform display autoscaling (scaling the smaller waveform to match
   the larger) may be disabled/enabled in the User Setup function.  Default
   setting is enabled ('ON').

5) Analog Conversion, Digital Oscilloscope, and Spectrum Analyzer support
   added for Motorola ADS board/Ariel ADC56000 combination.  Use "ADS56-A"
   designator inside System Configuration function (Workstation only).

6) Support added for Ariel DSPC25 board.  Use "ARI320-C" designator inside
   System Configuration function (Workstation only).  Although the maximum
   sampling rate for the Texas Instruments TLC32041 codec on this board is
   spec'ed at 19.2 KHz, some higher sampling rate values may work acceptably.

7) Onboard 8253 timer disabled between functions for Ariel DSP-16 operations
   to eliminate sampling frequency noise (Workstation only).


Workstation V1.95e, Plus V2.92e (22 JUL 89):

1) File capture option added to Time Display/Edit function.  Use by striking
   'w' key ('write') at anytime.  This option allows more convenient writing
   of waveform sections to separate output files than using combinations of
   the waveform editor Delete and Insert functions.

2) Previous beta version support of Loughborough Sound Images (Spectrum
   Signal Processing) Analog Devices ADSP-2100 card now included in standard
   distribution software.  Use "LSI21" as designator in System Configuration
   hardware selections (Workstation only).

3) Trace 2 scaling problem corrected with Ariel DSP-16 digital oscilloscope
   function (Workstation only).


Workstation V1.95f (10 AUG 89):

1) Support added for Ariel PC-56 DSP56001 board.  Default 56001 source code
   set for single-channel operation.  Use 'ARI56' as System Configuration
   designator.

2) Improvement made in DSP56001 code accelerated FFT processing magnitude
   approximation.  More exact magnitude results are returned from DSP56001
   processing (applies to all DSP56001-based boards).

3) Correction made to Acrosystems AT6400 INPUT GAIN LIST field for multiple
   channel gain entries.

4) Enhancements made to LSI Analog Devices ADSP-2100 board digital oscilloscope
   and spectrum analyzer functions.


Workstation V1.95g, Plus V2.92f (14 AUG 89):

1) Fix to File Acquisition function to correctly acquire files whose length
   are an exact multiple of 16384.

2) Spectrum Analyzer function added for Data Translation 282x hardware by
   using CAC WE DSP32 board (Workstation only).


Workstation V1.95h, Plus V2.92g (17 AUG 89):

1) Magnitude and 3-D Spectrogram display modified to correctly display
   "amplitude-squared" values on vertical axis.

2) Difference Equations modified to correctly evaluate output index in
   cases where lefthand side of equation contains frame-multiplier expressions
   such as y[0,n] or y[m\6,n].  Also, an "integer divide" function has been
   added--use the reverse slash character ('\').

3) Digital scope and spectrum analyzer functions have been modified to
   correctly display previously stored waveform files with the same amplitude
   scale as being used by the currently selected hardware (Workstation only).


Workstation V1.95i, Plus V2.92h (21 AUG 89):

1) File Acquisition modified to accept optional 'U' after format selection,
   allowing import of unsigned data.  Also, File Acquisition speed when
   writing output to disk increased.

2) Editor "undo" operation (when up or down cursor struck before carriage
   return on current field) made optional choice inside User Setup menu
   selection.

3) Undeclared rounding variable in Motorola DSP56001 IIR filter assembly code
   generation (for case of Q22 scaling only) corrected.  Also, rounding scheme
   changed to avoid use of long memory location (all non-Q23 scaling).

4) Difference Equations modified to allow "# of SAMPLES" field to be longer
   than the x1 and/or x2 input waveforms, as desired.  Useful for appending
   one waveform to another, frequency doubling, etc.


Workstation V1.95j, Plus V2.92i (30 AUG 89):

1) Further correction to unity gain calculation for IIR bandpass and bandstop
   filters, but only for elliptic and Chebyshev II designs (see Workstation
   V1.95d, Plus V2.92d, 12 JUL 89, above).

2) Correction to waveform editor "Write" function maximum amplitude calculation
   for output waveform when target window extends past end of input (displayed)
   waveform.

3) Addition of "MAX SCALE" parameter to time display, magnitude display, and
   3-D spectrogram display functions.  A non-zero entry defines the scale used
   along the y-axis, and along with the "scale factor" part of the Y LABELS
   field in these functions, allows wide flexibility for vertical axis
   scaling and units-per-division.  A zero entry (default) causes autoscaling
   to be in effect, where each waveform is shown to maximize display area
   usage.


Workstation V1.96a (8 SEP 89):

1) Fine-tuning of DSP56001 host-interface to avoid problems with some mask
   set DSP56001 chips (mask sets B77G and 2B3E) which could cause the Spectrum
   Analyzer and Digital Oscilloscope to hang-up.

2) Correction to playback from Waveform Display/Edit function for LSI DSP56001
   board.


Workstation V1.96b, Plus V2.92j (11 SEP 89):

1) Sign of denominator coefficients in IIR filter machine-generated source code
   header transfer function corrected to positive (comment only; not actual
   code).

2) '# of SAMPLES' field correction in Difference Equations--field is now
   completely independent of the length of the x1 and/or x2 waveforms, unless
   entered as zero.

3) Change to IIR filter structure #3 machine-generated "C" source code, where
   denominator ("B" array) coefficients were not being addressed correctly.

4) Correction to DSP56001 board digital oscilloscope displays, where display
   from waveform file only (no analog input) might have caused a run-time
   error (Workstation only).


Workstation V1.96c, Plus V2.93a (16 SEP 89):

1) Correction to Difference Equations output waveform file indexing problem
   at 4096 pt. boundaries when using x1 or x2 in equation.

2) Addition to Data Translation DT282x digital oscilloscope and spectrum
   analyzer functions to allow use of external trigger.  Use '+' and '-' keys
   inside these functions to control; "EXT" is displayed after current trigger
   trace when external trigger is active (Workstation only).

3) Addition to spectrum analyzer help explaining determination of maximum
   possible input value for log displays (Workstation only).

4) Increase in Ariel DSP-16 maximum acquisition rate, both for single-channel
   and dual-channel operation (Workstation only).


Workstation V1.96d (26 SEP 89):

1) Addition of LSI DSP32C board support.  Enter 'LSI32' in System Configuration
   function to enable functions that can use this board.  NOTE:  in tests with
   a pre-production DSP32C board, we found that on SOME systems enabling the
   80286 instruction set field in System Configuration (which directs the
   Hypersignal-Workstation real-time device drivers to use REP OUTSW and
   REP INSW 80286 instructions) can cause "scratches" or "spikes" in the
   incoming and outgoing data.  Also, we have found that these anomalies are
   sensitive to data amplitude levels; for example, nothing extraneous is
   present when outputting a waveform file of zeros, which indicates there
   may be a hardware problem.  We have found no such problems when the
   80286 instruction set is disabled, and, although maximum achievable
   real-time rates are less, we currently recommend this setting until the
   problem is solved.


Workstation V1.96e (31 OCT 89):

1) Correction to LSI DSP5600 board and Motorola ADS board (w/ Ariel ADC56000
   external analog I/O board option) two-channel operation.

2) Correction to automatic memory detection algorithm for DSP5600 boards with
   32K or greater 24-bit word memory (X: or Y:).

3) Improved robustness for CAC32 boards running in non-IBM clones.


*********** V2.00 released 1 MAR 90, see "addendum.doc" file ***********

Workstation V2.01, Plus V3.01 (20 APR 90):  SEE HS_REV2.DOC FILE
